WEBVTT

00:02.960 --> 00:04.020
Dear Mother,

00:04.410 --> 00:09.150
I have left the Dandelion Troupe and am heading towards England.

00:10.610 --> 00:16.290
Now I can meet with Applefield's director and have her testify that I am the real Nadja.

00:26.630 --> 00:27.790
NAAJA

00:26.630 --> 00:27.790
Nadja

00:27.820 --> 00:30.290
kimi no hitomi ni wa

00:27.840 --> 00:30.290
With your eyes

00:30.290 --> 00:31.450
NAAJA

00:30.340 --> 00:31.450
Nadja

00:31.470 --> 00:33.720
nani ga mieru

00:31.470 --> 00:33.720
What do you see?

00:33.940 --> 00:36.830
haruka tooku hikaru

00:33.940 --> 00:36.830
Shining in the far distance,

00:36.980 --> 00:39.120
mirai no tobira

00:36.980 --> 00:39.120
The door to the future,

00:40.260 --> 00:43.670
sagashiteiru

00:43.670 --> 00:50.880
Tomorrow's Nadja

00:55.100 --> 00:58.360
That's what I'm searching for

00:58.430 --> 01:01.810
minna egao de aetara

00:58.460 --> 01:01.810
I'm sure there would be no more fighting

00:58.920 --> 01:01.810
If everyone could meet with a smile

00:58.920 --> 01:01.810
arasoimo kitto nakunaru

01:01.840 --> 01:05.290
kon nani mo tanoshiku naru

01:01.840 --> 01:05.290
It could be so much more fun

01:05.660 --> 01:09.020
tabi no owari wa mienai

01:05.660 --> 01:09.020
I can't see the end of the journey

01:05.790 --> 01:08.920
sekai wa hiruikedo hitotsune

01:05.790 --> 01:08.920
The world is wide, but it's still one

01:09.050 --> 01:12.210
kamisama ga tabun shitteru

01:09.050 --> 01:12.210
To the people who, someday, I will meet again

01:09.390 --> 01:12.210
God is the only one who can possibly know

01:09.390 --> 01:12.210
itsukamata deaeru hito tachi ni

01:12.380 --> 01:16.030
te wo furinagara

01:12.380 --> 01:16.030
I will go waving

01:16.030 --> 01:18.180
toki ni wa BURUU ni naru himo aru kedo

01:16.030 --> 01:18.180
Sometimes, there are days I feel blue,

01:18.330 --> 01:25.070
ushiro mukanai

01:18.330 --> 01:25.070
But I won't look back

01:25.070 --> 01:27.810
yume ga kanau hima de

01:25.070 --> 01:27.810
Until the day my dream comes true

01:28.080 --> 01:33.120
NAAJA kimi no hoho emi wa

01:28.080 --> 01:33.120
Nadja, your smile

01:33.290 --> 01:36.670
NAAJA yuuki ni naru

01:33.290 --> 01:36.670
Nadja, you give me courage

01:36.750 --> 01:39.950
aoi sora no shita de

01:36.750 --> 01:39.950
Under the blue sky

01:40.250 --> 01:43.210
ashita no yukue

01:40.250 --> 01:43.210
I will find the place

01:43.190 --> 01:46.000
mitsu kerukara

01:43.190 --> 01:46.000
Where my future lies

01:46.520 --> 01:50.150
mitsu kerukara

01:46.520 --> 01:50.150
Where my future lies

02:00.430 --> 02:02.010
You are Nadja?

02:03.220 --> 02:03.910
Yes!

02:09.520 --> 02:10.310
Nadja!

02:10.680 --> 02:11.860
Mother!

02:24.180 --> 02:25.370
Francis!

02:25.880 --> 02:26.850
Keith!

02:33.340 --> 02:34.950
You've finally found your mother, haven't you?

02:35.070 --> 02:36.060
Congratulations.

02:39.290 --> 02:40.080
Thank you.

02:40.450 --> 02:42.080
Dance with me.

02:42.380 --> 02:43.830
No, dance with me first.

02:46.230 --> 02:49.040
I can't allow you to do that.

02:49.490 --> 02:52.500
If that's how it is...then Nadja, you choose.

02:52.700 --> 02:53.580
What!?

02:53.830 --> 02:56.500
E-even if you say that...what should I do?

02:56.690 --> 02:58.670
Um... what should I do?

02:58.770 --> 02:59.760
Ohhhh...

03:02.420 --> 03:03.630
Moo...?

03:07.780 --> 03:09.010
What's this?

03:25.000 --> 03:29.460
A Journey Alone with Joys and Hardships

03:35.990 --> 03:37.360
Sorry about that.

03:37.590 --> 03:37.960
Huh?

03:38.680 --> 03:40.730
That you had to sleep with the cow.

03:40.850 --> 03:43.150
Not at all! You really helped me out!

03:43.840 --> 03:49.660
If you want to go to England, the quickest way would be to take a ship from Cherbourg.

03:50.110 --> 03:50.970
Cherbourg?

03:51.470 --> 03:57.320
If you go there by train you'll be there in half a day. If you get on that ship, you'll be in England by tomorrow.

03:57.860 --> 03:58.230
Great!

04:00.130 --> 04:02.130
What!? It's not enough?

04:02.600 --> 04:05.240
It costs 1 franc to go to Cherbourg.

04:05.960 --> 04:08.180
Oh no, what should I do...

04:08.550 --> 04:11.390
Um, then please give me a ticket for however much I can afford with this.

04:11.880 --> 04:14.180
Well then, here's your ticket.

04:34.050 --> 04:38.000
I wonder which room I should use? Is anywhere okay?

04:40.590 --> 04:41.610
What is it?

04:41.830 --> 04:43.930
Ah, no...

04:44.350 --> 04:47.090
There aren't any more free seats, are there?

04:47.460 --> 04:48.620
Sorry for bothering you.

04:53.550 --> 04:55.230
Anyone here...?

04:55.700 --> 04:57.650
Ah, great!

04:58.150 --> 04:59.160
Wow

04:59.870 --> 05:01.750
Riding on a train is the best!

05:03.500 --> 05:04.710
Really now...

05:05.160 --> 05:06.710
I-I'm really sorry.

05:07.870 --> 05:10.490
I...I really didn't know.

05:10.980 --> 05:14.020
This isn't a place for a child like you.

05:14.690 --> 05:16.440
Please remove her already.

05:16.560 --> 05:18.140
I'm terribly sorry.

05:18.690 --> 05:19.280
Come on...

05:22.070 --> 05:23.750
You have third class seating.

05:24.070 --> 05:26.090
Go to the last car.

05:27.230 --> 05:27.820
Y-yes.

05:29.300 --> 05:40.730
Just like today, 100 years ago trains were divided up into first, second, and third class seating.

05:41.370 --> 05:45.320
Riding in the third class was normal to ordinary people.

05:46.630 --> 05:49.080
What in the world? They didn't have to go that far.

05:49.300 --> 05:50.430
How rude!

05:50.830 --> 05:52.060
Hm? Here?

05:54.900 --> 05:56.830
Huh? This is third class?

06:02.660 --> 06:03.940
Excuse me.

06:04.530 --> 06:06.140
Please let me through...

06:06.730 --> 06:08.140
Excuse me...

06:09.470 --> 06:11.620
Huh? It's full here too?

06:16.210 --> 06:17.020
Young lady!

06:18.580 --> 06:19.520
Over here!

06:19.890 --> 06:22.360
If it's just you, young lady, you can sit here.

06:26.800 --> 06:27.910
Thank you very much.

06:28.530 --> 06:30.870
Oh, you don't have to thank me.

06:33.910 --> 06:39.640
Even though I only borrowed one bottle of wine, my stupid...

06:40.900 --> 06:42.200
Are you listening, young lady?

06:42.200 --> 06:43.660
Huh!? Yes...

06:44.990 --> 06:47.960
Just recently a very beautiful girl...

06:48.330 --> 06:52.330
Ugh...I can't listen to him forever.

07:15.430 --> 07:16.400
Young lady.

07:17.460 --> 07:18.000
Yes?

07:19.260 --> 07:20.990
There's only one left, but would you like it?

07:21.090 --> 07:23.580
N-no, I'm fine.

07:26.720 --> 07:28.270
You don't have to hold back.

07:28.540 --> 07:31.280
Um...thank you very much.

07:32.590 --> 07:34.790
Well then, I'm going to go wash my hands.

07:35.040 --> 07:35.460
Okay.

07:37.280 --> 07:38.860
Time to eat!

07:40.100 --> 07:40.760
Huh?

07:42.120 --> 07:43.010
Who did that?

07:45.080 --> 07:47.110
W-what are you doing?

07:47.400 --> 07:48.000
Honestly!

07:50.590 --> 07:52.050
Do you have a problem with my son?

07:53.330 --> 07:55.630
Uh, no, nothing...

08:23.670 --> 08:25.300
Thief!

08:29.180 --> 08:30.340
That was close.

08:30.780 --> 08:33.200
Thank goodness I did what Thomas recommended.

08:35.770 --> 08:37.420
I haven't traveled far enough...

08:37.790 --> 08:38.580
What should I do...

08:39.520 --> 08:42.140
I wonder how far it is to Cherbourg?

08:43.400 --> 08:45.400
This won't be enough at all.

08:46.040 --> 08:46.510
Alright!

08:47.150 --> 08:52.210
...sings a song of love

08:52.680 --> 08:58.010
The wind blows gently in the pasture.

08:58.600 --> 09:03.320
All the little birds and young children,

09:03.740 --> 09:08.630
are held in their mother's embrace.

09:09.270 --> 09:14.480
The place where we play in our dreams,

09:14.820 --> 09:22.600
is a fragrant garden where the flowers bloom.

09:26.330 --> 09:31.540
Today's sun is passing us by...

09:32.030 --> 09:37.210
But I will hold its smiles in my hand.

09:37.610 --> 09:42.740
I say goodnight, I say goodnight...

09:43.070 --> 09:46.270
To this hand...

09:46.470 --> 09:51.730
My dear child...

09:56.350 --> 09:57.380
Thank you very much!

10:01.510 --> 10:03.580
Now I will make it to Cherbourg.

10:08.960 --> 10:10.860
I'll die!

10:14.290 --> 10:18.710
Catherine! Come back to me, or I really will jump!

10:18.860 --> 10:20.420
Go right ahead!

10:20.790 --> 10:22.540
I-if you want to stop me, you better do it now!

10:22.660 --> 10:25.210
Who would stop an idiot like you?

10:25.650 --> 10:27.820
Well then, do you need help, girl?

10:28.270 --> 10:29.500
U-um, actually...

10:29.530 --> 10:30.000
Move it!

10:38.070 --> 10:39.920
What are you doing, that was dangerous!

10:40.320 --> 10:41.650
I'm sorry.

10:41.770 --> 10:43.650
You really need to be more careful!

10:44.270 --> 10:46.730
It feels good to have helped somebody!

10:46.910 --> 10:47.920
It really does.

10:48.390 --> 10:49.200
Come on, let's go.

10:50.340 --> 10:51.940
Why did it turn out like this?

10:53.920 --> 10:55.940
Please let me see your tickets.

10:59.230 --> 11:00.070
Ticket check.

11:00.210 --> 11:01.000
Ah, yes.

11:05.000 --> 11:05.790
It's not there!

11:05.940 --> 11:06.630
Not there?

11:07.030 --> 11:09.620
Um...it was in my pocket...

11:14.480 --> 11:15.450
It was then...

11:17.890 --> 11:18.750
Please believe me.

11:19.250 --> 11:22.230
There's no mistaking it. I lost the ticket when I tried stopping the couple back here.

11:22.700 --> 11:23.670
Is that really true?

11:24.730 --> 11:25.470
It's true!

11:25.990 --> 11:30.310
There have been a lot of people who have been saying that recently.

11:30.630 --> 11:31.760
I'm different!

11:32.180 --> 11:33.000
Please believe me!

12:14.620 --> 12:15.710
I don't have any money.

12:15.820 --> 12:17.100
And no place to stay.

12:18.410 --> 12:19.440
What should I do?

12:26.880 --> 12:27.810
A secondhand shop.

12:29.520 --> 12:30.850
Um, excuse me!

12:32.480 --> 12:34.310
Sorry, but we are closed for the day.

12:35.370 --> 12:37.120
I don't have any money and I don't know what to do.

12:39.170 --> 12:42.130
Won't you buy something I own?

12:44.580 --> 12:46.530
It seems you have something valuable with you.

12:47.590 --> 12:51.070
Well now, I would buy that brooch for 60 franc.

12:51.560 --> 12:52.330
I can't sell this!

12:53.540 --> 12:56.620
I've had this ever since I was a baby. It's very precious to me.

12:57.190 --> 12:58.800
Then, do you have something else?

12:59.510 --> 13:00.280
I will look.

13:03.090 --> 13:04.060
Let's see...

13:05.170 --> 13:06.840
I can't sell my mother's dress.

13:07.490 --> 13:08.670
The kaleidoscope, too.

13:09.360 --> 13:11.760
The music box was a gift from Gerald...

13:13.630 --> 13:14.250
What about this?

13:15.310 --> 13:17.410
I'll only give you a few cents for that.

13:17.530 --> 13:19.950
Huh? That's not even enough to buy bread.

13:20.230 --> 13:22.770
That music box looks pretty nice.

13:22.970 --> 13:24.000
What? But...

13:25.190 --> 13:25.850
This is...

13:30.540 --> 13:31.430
As I thought...

13:32.590 --> 13:34.000
Can I take a look at it?

13:34.590 --> 13:35.410
Yes, of course.

13:41.530 --> 13:44.520
That's a pretty nice ornament.

13:48.810 --> 13:50.520
It's not too heavy.

13:54.990 --> 13:55.330
Huh?

13:56.270 --> 13:58.740
Young lady, where's the key to open this?

13:59.580 --> 14:00.440
A key?

14:03.110 --> 14:06.140
If there's no key, then I can't buy it.

14:06.690 --> 14:08.560
So, is there anything else besides the dress?

14:09.130 --> 14:10.020
There's nothing.

14:10.440 --> 14:11.800
Well, then it can't be helped.

14:12.710 --> 14:14.170
You should leave then.

14:16.710 --> 14:18.140
Now, that reminds me.

14:18.860 --> 14:23.920
I used to have a music box that was opened by a ring.

14:24.440 --> 14:25.250
A ring...?

14:25.650 --> 14:26.390
It can't be...

14:27.650 --> 14:28.860
But maybe...

14:30.880 --> 14:32.290
I won't know until I try.

14:39.650 --> 14:40.660
Ah, it opened!

14:41.000 --> 14:41.820
What is it?

14:46.210 --> 14:46.900
What's this?

14:53.250 --> 14:56.110
Oh-ho, these are real gold coins, miss.

14:56.700 --> 14:57.770
W-what should I do?

14:58.410 --> 14:59.490
What kind of thing is this?

14:59.960 --> 15:02.380
There's something written on that handkerchief.

15:02.650 --> 15:03.050
Huh?

15:03.910 --> 15:05.340
It's German.

15:05.540 --> 15:06.780
I wonder what the writing says.

15:07.540 --> 15:09.440
Dear Lady Colette,

15:09.640 --> 15:13.620
Please use this during troubled times. Edna.

15:15.050 --> 15:16.030
Colette?

15:20.400 --> 15:23.590
My mother was the previous owner of this?

15:24.480 --> 15:29.790
There's no mistake that the person who owned this music box and this brooch are one in the same.

15:30.300 --> 15:30.650
Really?

15:31.220 --> 15:32.990
The ornaments are the same.

15:33.590 --> 15:34.800
And look at this.

15:36.870 --> 15:37.830
I thought so!

15:39.220 --> 15:43.220
So Gerald bought this music box from my mother.

15:45.020 --> 15:49.490
Isn't that great, young lady? I can also buy those gold coins from you.

15:50.750 --> 15:52.150
Thank you very much.

15:55.190 --> 15:56.500
Ah, it's raining.

16:04.450 --> 16:05.110
What's wrong?

16:05.760 --> 16:06.720
Don't you have an umbrella?

16:08.250 --> 16:10.200
Let me take you home.

16:12.000 --> 16:12.670
It's okay!

16:19.480 --> 16:21.140
I guess I'm also very hungry.

16:21.580 --> 16:23.160
How about it? Let's eat something together.

16:25.550 --> 16:26.570
So, your mother...

16:28.170 --> 16:30.490
I want to meet my mother no matter what.

16:31.530 --> 16:32.490
I'm sure you will.

16:32.760 --> 16:33.700
Thank you, Jean!

16:34.170 --> 16:36.340
Ah, don't hold back. Help yourself.

16:36.740 --> 16:40.840
I'm full. Is it okay to bring this back home?

16:41.350 --> 16:43.160
I don't mind...but why?

16:43.900 --> 16:45.630
My mother is sick.

16:46.120 --> 16:48.910
So, I thought I'd give this to her.

16:51.200 --> 16:51.970
I see.

16:52.610 --> 16:54.320
You're thinking about your mother.

16:55.400 --> 16:57.480
I'll order more so you can take it home.

16:57.870 --> 17:00.640
It's okay! I can't eat anymore!

17:00.980 --> 17:03.450
And we've only just met today.

17:03.970 --> 17:06.170
What are you saying? We're already friends, right?

17:07.470 --> 17:08.260
Big sis...

17:09.150 --> 17:12.680
Is there anything else you want besides crepes? Like medicine?

17:13.700 --> 17:14.390
Is it okay?

17:14.710 --> 17:15.500
Of course!

17:19.400 --> 17:20.290
This much?

17:20.900 --> 17:23.990
I want to do something for someone who thinks of his mother.

17:24.680 --> 17:25.870
Thank you, sis!

17:27.370 --> 17:28.560
I'm going to buy medicine!

17:29.100 --> 17:30.680
Jean! The crepes, the crepes!

17:31.030 --> 17:32.680
Ah, I forgot.

17:40.580 --> 17:43.690
We know you have money. Be good and give it to us.

17:44.550 --> 17:45.490
N-no!

17:46.900 --> 17:47.740
Get it.

17:49.860 --> 17:50.970
Stop it!

17:51.340 --> 17:52.330
Let me go!

17:54.780 --> 17:55.270
Let's go.

17:56.920 --> 17:59.100
Come to think of it, that's a nice looking suitcase.

17:59.560 --> 18:01.100
Leave that alone!

18:04.430 --> 18:08.400
This is something that connects me and my mother together. It's more important than my life.

18:08.530 --> 18:09.860
That's enough.

18:10.820 --> 18:12.770
We already have her money. Let's go.

18:29.020 --> 18:29.780
Chief...

18:30.740 --> 18:31.730
Granny...

18:32.130 --> 18:33.070
Kennosuke...

18:33.630 --> 18:34.150
Rita...

18:35.140 --> 18:35.830
Abel...

18:36.350 --> 18:37.020
Sylvie...

18:37.440 --> 18:38.130
Thomas...

18:39.410 --> 18:41.340
I said I'd be fine alone, but...

18:42.450 --> 18:42.970
I...

18:56.520 --> 18:57.330
I'm home.

18:58.810 --> 18:59.800
Welcome back, big brother.

19:00.170 --> 19:03.280
I got paid extra at work.

19:03.700 --> 19:05.550
I got medicine and some fruit.

19:06.020 --> 19:07.580
Why so much?

19:09.380 --> 19:12.370
Like I said I got extra...

19:13.920 --> 19:14.960
Extra...?

19:15.750 --> 19:17.700
Alan, look into my eyes.

19:25.480 --> 19:26.460
No way, no way.

19:26.960 --> 19:28.590
Please, I have to go to England no matter what!

19:29.200 --> 19:29.950
Please!

19:30.270 --> 19:31.250
Let me on!

19:31.530 --> 19:33.150
Then give me the money!

19:33.430 --> 19:35.380
I'll wash the dishes. I'll do anything!

19:35.750 --> 19:38.640
That's not good enough. Go home!

19:40.170 --> 19:40.910
Hmph.

19:41.350 --> 19:43.990
I'll get to England no matter what.

19:44.510 --> 19:45.300
As if I'll be beaten by this!

20:26.580 --> 20:28.330
I don't need a hat.

20:28.900 --> 20:31.100
T-that's not what I meant...

20:31.340 --> 20:33.320
Would you mind giving me some money to buy bread?

20:34.730 --> 20:36.970
I don't have any money either.

20:37.470 --> 20:38.970
Well, that's terrible.

20:39.290 --> 20:41.440
Everyone, another round of applause!

20:43.020 --> 20:44.380
T-thanks.

20:47.960 --> 20:50.480
Well...it doesn't seem like I'll get any money...

20:57.910 --> 20:58.870
Sis.

21:00.050 --> 21:01.260
Ah, you are...

21:01.590 --> 21:02.380
I'm sorry.

21:02.700 --> 21:03.910
Jean, what are you talking about?

21:04.300 --> 21:08.500
The ones who stole your money were my big brother and his friends.

21:08.820 --> 21:09.630
Forgive me.

21:10.100 --> 21:11.830
I wanted to buy medicine for my mother.

21:12.550 --> 21:13.440
So that was it.

21:14.270 --> 21:15.950
I heard the story from Jean.

21:16.420 --> 21:19.060
You're traveling so you can meet your mother, right?

21:20.840 --> 21:21.240
Yeah.

21:21.730 --> 21:24.000
I already spent the money I took but...

21:24.520 --> 21:26.540
I'll help you however I can!

21:27.190 --> 21:29.310
I want to go to England.

21:29.950 --> 21:31.900
Is that all? That's easy.

21:32.100 --> 21:32.400
Huh?

21:33.040 --> 21:34.720
But I don't have any...

21:35.040 --> 21:36.170
Leave it to me.

21:36.770 --> 21:39.550
I have a friend who is a member of that ship's crew.

21:43.830 --> 21:46.570
It's a bit narrow, but please hang in there.

21:46.910 --> 21:48.390
Thank you, everyone!

21:51.870 --> 21:53.820
Be careful, big sis.

21:54.120 --> 21:56.810
I hope you can meet your mother.

21:57.550 --> 21:58.070
Yes!

21:59.450 --> 22:08.120
And so, Nadja is heading back to England so she can meet with the director of Applefield.

22:14.690 --> 22:17.950
RONDON donyori haretara PARI

22:14.690 --> 22:17.950
Paris is sunnier than London

22:18.080 --> 22:21.140
KARUMEN menyori PAERIYA suki

22:18.080 --> 22:21.140
Carmen likes paella more than pasta

22:21.510 --> 22:27.780
SUPEEDO no jyoou kimagure yasan

22:21.510 --> 22:27.780
The Queen of Spades is a fickle person

22:28.690 --> 22:29.950
kitto

22:28.690 --> 22:29.950
Indeed

22:32.710 --> 22:35.140
nayan datte muda yo

22:32.710 --> 22:35.140
It's no use worrying about it

22:35.190 --> 22:38.840
kesera sera sera sera

22:35.190 --> 22:38.840
Que sera sera, sera sera

22:39.040 --> 22:43.770
